  "appreciation": "本诗出自《诗经·魏风》，以“比”体将贪婪的剥削者化为偷食的硕鼠，形象贴切且饱含愤懑。重章叠句的结构不仅增强了诗歌的音乐节奏感，更层层递进地控诉了剥削者的冷酷无情。从“无食我黍”到“无食我麦”“无食我苗”，写尽了劳动者辛勤成果被掠夺的无奈；从“适彼乐土”到“乐国”“乐郊”的向往，则展现了先民反抗压迫、追求无剥削理想社会的觉醒。全诗情感由怨愤转为决绝，质朴中透出强烈的反抗精神。",
  "english": "Large rats, large rats, / Eat not our millet! / Three years we have served you, / Yet you will not look on us. / We swear to leave you, / And go to that happy land. / Happy land, happy land, / There we shall find our place. / Large rats, large rats, / Eat not our wheat! / Three years we have served you, / Yet you show no gratitude. / We swear to leave you, / And go to that happy state. / Happy state, happy state, / There we shall find our due. / Large rats, large rats, / Eat not our seedlings! / Three years we have served you, / Yet you give us no comfort. / We swear to leave you, / And go to those happy fields. / Happy fields, happy fields, / Who there would ever wail?",
  "source": "chinese-poetry",
