  "appreciation": "本诗是《大雅》名篇，颂周文王之德与周代殷而立的天命。全诗以“天命”为线索，首尾呼应，通过文王“陟降在帝左右”的神化描写，确立周统的合法性。诗人并未止于赞美，而是借殷商子孙臣服的景象，发出“天命靡常”的警示，劝勉周人修德求福、“宜鉴于殷”。艺术上，全诗气魄宏大，章法严密，设问与感叹的运用增强了感染力，尤其“周虽旧邦，其命维新”更成千古名句，兼具颂歌的庄重与政治哲理的深邃。",
  "english": "King Wen is on high, oh, shining in the sky. / Though Zhou is an old state, its mandate is renewed. / The glory of Zhou is manifest, God's mandate is timely. / King Wen ascends and descends, at God's side. / Diligent is King Wen, his good fame endless. / He bestowed gifts to establish Zhou, making his descendants lords. / King Wen's descendants, main and branch lines for a hundred generations, / all Zhou's officers, their glory lasts for generations. / Their glory lasting for generations, their plans are cautious and careful. / Thinking of these fine men, born in this kingdom. / The kingdom is able to produce them, they are Zhou's pillars; / With these numerous fine men, King Wen rests in peace. / August is King Wen, continuously bright and reverent. / Great is the mandate of Heaven! Over Shang's descendants. / Shang's descendants, their number is not less than a hundred million. / Since God has given the mandate, they become vassals to Zhou. / Serving as vassals to Zhou, the mandate of Heaven is not constant. / The officers of Yin are capable and quick. / They perform the libation in the capital. / When they perform the libation, they wear their embroidered robes and caps. / O king's faithful ministers, do not forget your ancestors. / Do not forget your ancestors, cultivate your virtue. / Forever align with the mandate, seek many blessings for yourselves. / Before Yin lost the multitudes, they could align with God. / Take Yin as a mirror, the great mandate is not easy to keep! / The mandate is not easy to keep, do not let it end in your person. / Proclaim your righteous fame, observe Yin's fate from Heaven. / The doings of high Heaven, have neither sound nor smell. / Take King Wen as your model, and all states will trust in you.",
  "source": "chinese-poetry",
