  "appreciation": "本篇极写深山幽谷的险恶环境，借以劝唤隐士早日归返。全诗采用铺陈夸饰手法，生动描绘桂树盘绕、山石嵯峨、猿狖悲鸣、虎豹争斗的悚然景象，营造出幽深可怖的意境。句式多用“兮”字，音调急促跌宕，与惊惧情感相呼应。篇中“王孙游兮不归，春草生兮萋萋”于繁密险恶中忽作清丽悠远之语，形成强烈反差，既流露思归之情，又以凄美景致反衬山中不可久留的主旨，情景交融，动人心魄。",
  "english": "Sweet laurels cluster in the mountain's deep gloom, / Their branches twist and intertwine. / Mountain vapors soar, rocks tower steep, / Ravines are sheer, waters ripple in layers. / Apes and monkeys howl, tigers and leopards roar, / Clinging to laurel branches, I linger a while. / The noble prince wanders and returns not, / Spring grass grows lush and green. / At year's end, I find no solace, / Cicadas chirp mournfully. / The mountains roll and bend, / My lingering heart is lost in dread. / Bewildered and submerged in fear, / For these are the dens of tigers and leopards. / In the thickets and deep woods, / Men would tremble to ascend. / The crags are jagged and steep, / Roots tangle, forest timbers twist. / Green sedge grows mixed among trees, / Fen grass sways in the wind. / White deer and stags, / Some leap, some rest. / The peaks loom high and grand, / Chilly and damp the air. / Macaques and mighty bears, / Lament for their kind in sorrow. / Clinging to laurel branches, I linger a while. / Tigers and leopards fight, bears roar, / Beasts panic and flee their flocks. / O prince, return! / The mountains are no place to linger long.",
  "source": "chinese-poetry",
