  "appreciation": "本篇为《楚辞·九怀》之七，借悲秋抒发怀才不遇与思君恋国之幽情。开篇以秋风、微霜、病蝉、归鸟等凄凉意象起兴，渲染肃杀氛围，暗喻时局衰败与贤臣遭弃。中段以“临渊”“顾林”写现实荒凉，复借“骑霓”“乘云”展现神游天界、自强不息的孤高理想。然终以“失志”“思君”跌回现实，神游难掩尘世之悲。全诗浪漫想象与现世沉沦交织，将去国怀乡之痛与忠贞不渝之节熔铸一炉，深得屈子遗风。",
  "english": "The autumn wind sighs and whistles, / Spreading fragrant blooms and swaying boughs. / A faint frost fills the boundless sky, / Dying cicadas chirp their mournful cries. / The swallows bid farewell and fly away, / Soaring toward the sacred hills. / I gaze at mist-shrouded valleys deep, / Where bears and boars roar fierce and wild. / The sage days of Tang and Yu are no more, / Why do I linger here so long? / Facing the abyss, the waters are vast, / Looking back at the woods, all is wild and bare. / I arrange my robes of flowing grace, / Mount the rainbow to soar to the south. / Riding the clouds in swirling flight, / I press on tirelessly, striving in might. / I seek rest by the orchid-fringed shore, / But lost in purpose, my thoughts drift afar. / Grief festers, leaving my face dark and worn, / Yearning for my lord in endless woe. / My body departs, yet my heart remains, / Filled with sorrow and bitter pain.",
  "source": "chinese-poetry",
