  "appreciation": "本篇借凭吊屈原以抒发自身愤懑。开篇直抒胸臆，痛悼屈原沉江，继而揭露楚国政坛黑白颠倒、贤愚错位的浊世。诗人以“殦雕游华屋，鵔鸃栖柴蔟”的鲜明对比，刺透贤才被弃的荒谬。中段笔锋一转，以奇幻的游仙之笔写乘云升天、问路星辰，展现超越尘世的追求。然天界亦非坦途，御者迷轨，求索不耦，终以“攀天阶下视”折返故国，却见群小沓沓。全篇想象瑰丽，虚实交织，将神游的旷达与坠入现实的悲怆强烈对立，深刻道出高洁之士进退失据的孤独与哀痛。",
  "english": "Lamenting Qu Yuan’s bitter fate, / A royal body sank in Xiang and Milo. / Why is Chu so hard to transform, / Remaining unchanged to this very day? / Scholars lack the will for noble ways, / Vying in flattery and slanderous strife. / Calling true justice twisted and wrong, / Slandering fine jade as worthless stone. / Owls and vultures roam in grand halls, / While golden pheasants perch on thorny faggots. / I rouse myself to swiftly flee, / Shunning the insults of the petty crowd. / Riding blue clouds I soar on high, / Toward the realm of radiant light. / Treading heaven’s path I drive straight on, / Following the nine suns to sport and play. / Crossing the Milky Way to the southern shore, / Grazing my horse by the Altair star. / Clouds and rainbows darken the firmament, / Stars of Shen and Chen turn upside down. / Meeting a shooting star I ask the way, / It points me leftward with its gleam. / Driving straight toward the Juzi stars, / My charioteer loses track and swerves. / Stumbling astray on a wandering path, / My course diverges from sun and moon. / My will blocked, where can I go? / Grieving that my quest meets no accord. / Climbing heaven’s stairs I gaze below, / And see old home in Yan and Ying. / My heart roams free, I long to return, / But filthy crowds swarm endlessly. / Sorrow chokes me, twisting my thoughts, / Tears stream down like pouring rain.",
