  "text": "子张问于孔子曰：“何如斯可以从政矣？”子曰：“尊五美，屏四恶，斯可以从政矣。”子张曰：“何谓五美？”子曰：“君子惠而不费，劳而不怨，欲而不贪，泰而不骄，威而不猛。”子张曰：“何谓惠而不费？”子曰：“因民之所利而利之，斯不亦惠而不费乎？择可劳而劳之，又谁怨？欲仁而得仁，又焉贪？君子无众寡，无小大，无敢慢，斯不亦泰而不骄乎？君子正其衣冠，尊其瞻视，俨然人望而畏之，斯不亦威而不猛乎？”子张曰：“何谓四恶？”子曰：“不教而杀谓之虐；不戒视成谓之暴；慢令致期谓之贼；犹之与人也，出纳之吝谓之有司。”",
  "pinyin": "zi zhāng wèn yú kǒng zi yuē ： “ hé rú sī kě yǐ cóng zhèng yǐ ？ ” zi yuē ： “ zūn wǔ měi ， píng sì è ， sī kě yǐ cóng zhèng yǐ 。 ” zi zhāng yuē ： “ hé wèi wǔ měi ？ ” zi yuē ： “ jūn zǐ huì ér bù fèi ， láo ér bù yuàn ， yù ér bù tān ， tài ér bù jiāo ， wēi ér bù měng 。 ” zi zhāng yuē ： “ hé wèi huì ér bù fèi ？ ” zi yuē ： “ yīn mín zhī suǒ lì ér lì zhī ， sī bù yì huì ér bù fèi hū ？ zé kě láo ér láo zhī ， yòu shuí yuàn ？ yù rén ér dé rén ， yòu yān tān ？ jūn zǐ wú zhòng guǎ ， wú xiǎo dà ， wú gǎn màn ， sī bù yì tài ér bù jiāo hū ？ jūn zǐ zhèng qí yī guān ， zūn qí zhān shì ， yǎn rán rén wàng ér wèi zhī ， sī bù yì wēi ér bù měng hū ？ ” zi zhāng yuē ： “ hé wèi sì è ？ ” zi yuē ： “ bù jiào ér shā wèi zhī nüè ； bù jiè shì chéng wèi zhī bào ； màn lìng zhì qī wèi zhī zéi ； yóu zhī yǔ rén yě ， chū nà zhī lìn wèi zhī yǒu sī 。 ”",
  "translation": "子张问孔子说：",
  "notes": [
   {
    "term": "惠而不费",
    "explain": "施惠于民而不耗费自己的财力，指顺应百姓自身可获利之处加以引导"
   },
   {
    "term": "泰而不骄",
    "explain": "泰，安泰舒泰。君子无论人多人少、事大事小皆不敢怠慢，故安泰而不骄纵"
   },
   {
    "term": "不戒视成",
    "explain": "不事先告诫便要求其完成，指不给予准备和训导便苛求成效"
   },
   {
    "term": "慢令致期",
    "explain": "政令下达迟缓，却限期完成，指命令前后矛盾而苛责百姓"
   },
   {
    "term": "有司",
    "explain": "本指具体管事的低级官吏，此指格局狭小、吝于付出的做派"
   }
  ],
  "appreciation": "本章以问答对话展开，层次分明，逻辑严密。孔子先总提",
  "english": "Zizhang asked Confucius: \"What must one do to govern effectively?\" / Confucius said: \"Honor the five virtues, reject the four evils—then you may govern.\" / Zizhang said: \"What are the five virtues?\" / Confucius said: \"A gentleman benefits the people without waste, / labors them without resentment, / desires without greed, / is composed without arrogance, / inspires awe without fierceness.\" / Zizhang said: \"What is to benefit without waste?\" / Confucius said: \"To guide the people toward what naturally profits them—is this not benefiting without waste? / To choose labors fitting for the people and then assign them—who would resent it? / To desire benevolence and attain it—where is the greed? / Whether dealing with many or few, great or small, never presuming to be negligent—is this not composure without arrogance? / To keep one's garments proper, maintain a dignified bearing, so that people look upon him with reverence—is this not authority without fierceness?\" / Zizhang said: \"What are the four evils?\" / Confucius said: \"To execute without first instructing—this is tyranny. / To demand results without prior warning—this is violence. / To issue orders slowly yet impose strict deadlines—this is treachery. / Even when bestowing rewards upon others, to be stingy in distribution—this is pettiness.\"",
  "source": "chinese-poetry",
