  "appreciation": "此章以恢弘之笔赞颂孔子之德与天地之道相配。作者连用“天地”“四时”“日月”等宏大意象，极言孔子之道无所不包、生生不息。排比与比喻交织，气势磅礴而不失醇厚。“万物并育而不相害，道并行而不相悖”一句，道出儒家包容和谐、和而不同的至高境界。小德如川流不息，大德则厚德载物，动静相宜，微观与宏观统一，尽显天地之大德，亦为儒者理想人格之极致写照。",
  "english": "Zhongni traced the ways of Yao and Shun, / And modeled himself on Wen and Wu. / Above, he followed the seasons of Heaven; / Below, he adapted to the nature of water and earth. / He is like Heaven and Earth, holding and bearing all things, / Covering and sheltering all without exception. / Like the alternating course of the four seasons, / Like the alternating brightness of the sun and moon. / All things grow together without harming one another, / The great Ways run parallel without conflicting. / Minor virtues flow like rivers, / Major virtues are solid and transforming. / This is why Heaven and Earth are so great.",
  "source": "chinese-poetry",
